 ( { Should White advance with } 0... Re6 0. f5 { , or would they be better off keeping the central tension with } 1. O-O $2 ) 
1. { -KEY- } f5 $1 { Correct! Here this move is very strong. The most important thing about this move is that it stops Black from playing ...exf4, which means that Black is left with a very passive dark-squared bishop. Unfortunately for Black, all of their minor pieces have now become very passive. } ( 1. O-O $6 { still keeps an objective advantage, but it does allow Black to ease some of the pressure by playing } exf4 $1 { when after } 2. Bxf4 Nd4 { Black has succeeded in exchanging not only one set of pawns, but is now forcing an exchange of a set of minor pieces. } ) 
Nd4 { A natural move, attempting to exchange off a few pieces to try to ease some of the problems of having less space. } 2. O-O ( { The threat is } 2. O-O -- 3. f6 { next. } ) 
Nec6 3. g5 $1 { Grabbing even more space! } Nxe2+ { Black continues their strategy of exchanging pieces. } ( 3... gxf5 $2 4. exf5 { and now the pawn on f5 cannot be captured, because of the pressure against the knight on c6. After } Bxf5 5. Bxc6 Nxc6 6. Rxf5 $18 { White emerges up a full piece. } ) 
4. Qxe2 Nd4 5. Qf2 $18 { It is no exaggeration to say that White is already objectively winning. Black's bishops both remain passive, while White has a devastating attack on the kingside. To add insult to injury, the pawn on h4 is a constant problem that prevents Black from being able to castle short. The only black piece that 'looks good' is the knight on d4, but even here White has arranged their pieces very well and effectively neutralized its influence on the game. This example is a typical one, and a good illustration of how quickly you can collapse your opponent's position when you grab space with many pieces still remaining on the board. This brings us to the end of this section. In the next section, we'll expand on the coverage of the space advantage, and introduce several typical techniques that you can aim for when you are the side with more space. } 
